{"block_id": "ch29-b0001", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "ad51aa50aadbc170", "translated": "纵观全书，我们从智能体式 AI 的基础概念出发，一路走到复杂自主系统的实际实现。我们开篇便提出一个前提：构建智能体类似于在一块技术画布上创作一件复杂的艺术作品——这一过程不仅需要一个强大的认知引擎，例如大语言模型，还需要一套稳健的架构蓝图。这些蓝图（即智能体式设计模式）为将简单、被动响应的模型转变为主动、以目标为导向、能够进行复杂推理与行动的实体，提供了所需的结构与可靠性。\n\n本结语章将综合我们已探讨的核心原则。我们将首先回顾关键的智能体式设计模式，将它们归并为一个有凝聚力的框架，以凸显其整体重要性。接下来，我们将考察如何将这些独立模式组合成更复杂的系统，从而产生强大的协同效应。最后，我们将展望智能体开发的未来，探索将塑造下一代智能体系统的 emerging 趋势与挑战。\n\n> **注**：原文 \"emerging trends\" 未完整结尾即在块边界截断，仅按原文翻译至该处。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:35.569237", "block_id": "ch29-b0001", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 515, "output_tokens": 197, "elapsed_sec": 4.11, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0002", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "fe3d998c86027ff7", "translated": "## 核心智能体式原则回顾\n\n本指南详细阐述的 21 个模式构成了一个全面的智能体开发工具集。每个模式虽然各自针对特定的设计挑战,但可以按照反映智能体核心能力的基础类别进行整体理解。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:37.272517", "block_id": "ch29-b0002", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4406, "output_tokens": 49, "elapsed_sec": 1.7, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0003", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "553b4dd6bbfca0d7", "translated": "## 组合模式以构建复杂系统\n\n智能体式设计的真正力量,不在于孤立地应用单一模式,而在于巧妙地将多个模式组合起来,创建出复杂的多层系统。智能体式画布很少由单一、简单的工作流构成;相反,它会演变成一幅由相互连接的模式交织而成的画卷,这些模式协同工作以达成复杂目标。设想开发一个自主人工智能研究助手,这一任务需要结合规划、信息检索、分析与综合。这类系统正是模式组合的典型范例:\n\n- **初始规划**:用户查询(例如\"分析量子计算对网络安全领域的影响\")首先由规划器智能体接收。该智能体将运用规划模式,将高层级请求分解为结构化的多步骤研究计划。该计划可能包含如下步骤:\"识别量子计算的基础概念\"\"研究常见的密码学算法\"\"查找针对密码学的量子威胁的专家分析\",以及\"将发现综合为结构化报告\"。\n\n- **结合工具使用的信息收集**:为执行该计划,智能体将主要依赖工具使用模式。计划的每一步都会触发对 Google Search 或 vertex_ai_search 工具的调用。对于更结构化的数据,它可能会使用工具来查询 ArXiv 等学术数据库或金融数据 API。\n\n- **协作分析与写作**:单个智能体或许能够处理这一任务,但更稳健的架构会采用多智能体协作模式。一个\"研究员\"智能体可负责执行搜索计划并收集原始信息。其输出(即一系列摘要与来源链接)随后会被传递给一个\"写作\"智能体。该专业智能体将以初始计划为大纲,把所收集的信息综合为一份连贯的初稿。\n\n- **迭代反思与优化**:初稿鲜有完美……", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:41.689504", "block_id": "ch29-b0003", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4721, "output_tokens": 341, "elapsed_sec": 4.42, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0004", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "69bc092631a75735", "translated": "这个专业智能体(Agent)以初始规划作为大纲,将收集到的信息合成为一份连贯的草稿。\n\n- 迭代式反思与精炼:初稿很少是完美的。反思(Reflection)模式可以通过引入第三个\"评审器(Critic)\"智能体来实现。该智能体的唯一职责是审阅写作智能体的草稿,检查逻辑矛盾、事实错误或表述不清之处。其评审意见会反馈给写作智能体,由写作智能体利用自我修正(Self-Correction)模式对输出进行精炼,吸纳反馈以产出更高质量的最终报告。\n- 状态管理:在整个流程中,记忆管理(Memory Management)系统不可或缺。它负责维护研究规划的状态,存储检索器收集的信息,保存写作智能体创建的草稿,并跟踪来自评审器的反馈,从而确保在多步骤、多智能体工作流的整个过程中上下文得以保留。在该示例中,至少融合了五种不同的智能体式(Agentic)模式。规划(Planning)模式提供高层结构,工具使用(Tool Use)将操作锚定在真实世界数据之上,多智能体协作(Multi-Agent Collaboration)促成专业化分工,反思保证质量,而记忆管理维持一致性。这种组合将一组独立的能力转化为一个强大的自主系统,使其能够处理对单次提示(Prompt)或简单链而言过于复杂的任务。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:46.061566", "block_id": "ch29-b0004", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4663, "output_tokens": 270, "elapsed_sec": 4.37, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0005", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "b13737eea6ce3665", "translated": "## 展望未来\n\n正如我们的 AI 研究助手所展示的，将智能体式(Agentic)模式组合成复杂系统并非故事的终点，而是软件开发新篇章的起点。展望未来，若干新兴趋势和挑战将定义下一代智能系统的形态，突破当前的能力边界，并对其设计者提出更高的要求。\n\n通往更高级智能体式 AI 的旅程将以对更高自主性与推理能力的追求为标志。我们所讨论的这些模式为目标导向的行为提供了脚手架，但未来还需要能够应对歧义、执行抽象与因果推理、甚至展现一定常识的智能体。这很可能涉及与新型模型架构以及神经符号方法的更紧密结合——后者将大语言模型(LLM)的模式匹配优势与经典 AI 的逻辑严谨性融为一体。我们将看到从人在回路(Human-in-the-Loop)系统（智能体扮演副驾驶角色）向人在回路上(Human-on-the-Loop)系统的转变——后者中智能体被信任以最少监督执行复杂、长期运行的任务，仅在目标完成或发生关键异常时才回报。\n\n这一演进将伴随着智能体生态系统与标准化的兴起。多智能体协作(Multi-Agent Collaboration)模式凸显了专用智能体的强大威力，而未来将出现开放的市场和平台，使开发者能够部署、发现并编排作为服务交付的智能体舰队。要使这一愿景成为现实，模型上下文协议(Model Context Protocol, MCP)与智能体到智能体(A2A)背后的原则将变得至关重要，并促成业界广泛的标准，规定智能体、工具与模型之间如何交换的不仅是数据，还包括上下文、目标与能力。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:49.503866", "block_id": "ch29-b0005", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4723, "output_tokens": 320, "elapsed_sec": 3.44, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0006", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "d34a2953bdb0ad07", "translated": "这个不断壮大的生态系统中,一个典型的例子就是 \"Awesome Agents\" GitHub 仓库。这是一个极具价值的资源,作为一个精心整理的开源 AI 智能体、框架和工具列表,它展示了该领域的快速创新,涵盖了从软件开发到自主研究和对话式 AI 等各种前沿项目。然而,这条道路并非没有艰巨的挑战。随着智能体变得更加自主且相互关联,安全性、对齐和鲁棒性等核心问题将变得愈发关键。我们如何确保智能体的学习与适应不会导致其偏离最初的目标？我们如何构建能够抵御对抗性攻击和不可预测的真实世界场景的系统？回答这些问题将需要一套新的\"安全模式(Safety Patterns)\",以及一套严谨的工程规范,聚焦于测试、验证和伦理对齐。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:51.951249", "block_id": "ch29-b0006", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4531, "output_tokens": 150, "elapsed_sec": 2.45, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0007", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "066b8ba38dd80919", "translated": "## 结语\n\n贯穿本指南,我们一直将智能体的构建视为在一块技术画布上施展的艺术。这些智能体设计模式(Agentic Design Patterns)正是你的调色板与笔触:它们是使你能够超越简单提示、创造动态、响应式且目标导向的实体的基础要素。它们提供了将大语言模型的原始认知能力转化为可靠且有目的系统所需的架构纪律。\n\n真正的技艺不在于掌握单一模式,而在于理解它们之间的相互作用:将整块画布视为一个整体,构建一个让规划、工具使用、反思与协作和谐共生的系统。智能体式设计的原则是一种全新创造语言的语法,它使我们能够不仅告诉机器\"做什么\",还能告诉机器\"如何成为\"。\n\n智能体式人工智能是当今技术领域中最激动人心且发展最为迅速的领域之一。本书所详述的概念与模式并非某种终极、静态的教条,而是一个起点——一个坚实的基础,供你在其上构建、试验与创新。未来的图景中,我们不仅仅是人工智能的使用者,更是智能系统的架构师,这些系统将助力我们解决世界上最复杂的问题。画布就在你眼前,模式已在你手中。现在,是时候动手构建了。\n\n## 术语表", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:54.362414", "block_id": "ch29-b0007", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4644, "output_tokens": 248, "elapsed_sec": 2.41, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0008", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "c2931d81a5bd37f7", "translated": "# Glossary\n\n## Fundamental Concepts\n\n**Prompt** A prompt is the input, typically in the form of a question, instruction, or statement, that a user provides to an AI model to elicit a response. The quality and structure of the prompt heavily influence the model's output, making prompt engineering a key skill for effectively using AI.\n\n**Context Window** The context window is the maximum number of tokens an AI model can process at once, including both the input and its generated output. This fixed size is a critical limitation, as information outside the window is ignored, while larger windows enable more complex conversations and document analysis.\n\n**In-Context Learning** In-context learning is an AI's ability to learn a new task from examples provided directly in the prompt, without requiring any retraining. This powerful feature allows a single, general-purpose model to be adapted to countless specific tasks on the fly.\n\n**Zero-Shot, One-Shot, and Few-Shot Prompting** These are prompting techniques where a model is given zero, one, or a few examples of a task to guide its response. Providing more examples generally helps the model better understand the user's intent and improves its accuracy for the specific task.\n\n**Multimodality** Multimodality is an AI's ability to understand and process information across multiple data types like text, images, and audio. This allows for more versatile and human-like interactions, such as describing an image or answering a spoken question.\n\n**Grounding** Grounding is the process of connecting a model's outputs to verifiable, real-world information sources to ensure factual accuracy and reduce hallucinations.", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:25:56.916914", "block_id": "ch29-b0008", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4689, "output_tokens": 321, "elapsed_sec": 2.55, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0009", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "f30e4592d5766dc2", "translated": "## 核心 AI 模型架构\n\n**Transformer** Transformer 是大多数现代大语言模型的基础神经网络架构。其核心创新在于自注意力机制(self-attention),能够高效处理长文本序列,并捕捉词与词之间的复杂关系。\n\n**循环神经网络(Recurrent Neural Network, RNN)** 循环神经网络是 Transformer 之前的基础架构。RNN 顺序处理信息,通过循环维持对先前输入的\"记忆\",因此适用于文本和语音处理等任务。\n\n**混合专家模型(Mixture of Experts, MoE)** 混合专家模型是一种高效的模型架构,由一个\"路由器\"网络动态选取少量\"专家\"网络来处理任意给定输入。这使得模型能够在保持可管理计算成本的同时拥有海量参数。\n\n**扩散模型(Diffusion Models)** 扩散模型是擅长生成高质量图像的生成模型。它们的工作方式是对数据添加随机噪声,然后训练模型精确地逆转该过程,从而能够从随机起点生成新数据。\n\n**Mamba** Mamba 是近期出现的 AI 架构,采用选择性状态空间模型(Selective State Space Model, SSM)高效处理序列,尤其适用于极长上下文。其选择性机制使其能够聚焦相关信息、过滤噪声,有望成为 Transformer 的替代方案。", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:26:00.196979", "block_id": "ch29-b0009", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4640, "output_tokens": 242, "elapsed_sec": 3.28, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0010", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "383b7d71f3efac7a", "translated": "**The LLM Development Lifecycle**[^1]\n\n**Pre-training Techniques** Pre-training is the initial phase where a model learns general knowledge from vast amounts of data. The top techniques for this involve different objectives for the model to learn from. The most common is Causal Language Modeling (CLM), where the model predicts the next word in a sentence. Another is Masked Language Modeling (MLM), where the model fills in intentionally hidden words in a text. Other important methods include Denoising Objectives, where the model learns to restore a corrupted input to its original state, Contrastive Learning, where it learns to distinguish between similar and dissimilar pieces of data, and Next Sentence Prediction (NSP), where it determines if two sentences logically follow each other.\n\n**Fine-tuning Techniques** Fine-tuning is the process of adapting a general pre-trained model to a specific task using a smaller, specialized dataset. The most common approach is Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT), where the model is trained on labeled examples of correct input-output pairs. A popular variant is Instruction Tuning, which focuses on training the model to better follow user commands.\n\n[^1]: The development of a powerful language model follows a distinct sequence. It begins with Pre-training, where a massive base model is built by training it on a vast dataset of general internet text to learn language, reasoning, and world knowledge. Next is Fine-tuning, a specialization phase where the general model is further trained on smaller, task-specific datasets to adapt its capabilities for a particular purpose. The final stage is Alignment, where the specialized model's behavior is adjusted to ensure its outputs are helpful, harmless, and aligned with human values.", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:26:02.505343", "block_id": "ch29-b0010", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4712, "output_tokens": 335, "elapsed_sec": 2.31, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0011", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "291750323365066e", "translated": "To make this process more efficient, Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) methods are used, with top techniques including LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation), which only updates a small number of parameters, and its memory-optimized version, QLoRA. Another technique, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), enhances the model by connecting it to an external knowledge source during the fine-tuning or inference stage.\n\n## Alignment and Safety Techniques\n\nAlignment is the process of ensuring an AI model's behavior aligns with human values and expectations, making it helpful and harmless. The most prominent technique is Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF), where a \"reward model\" trained on human preferences guides the AI's learning process, often using an algorithm like Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) for stability. Simpler alternatives have emerged, such as Direct Preference Optimization (DPO), which bypasses the need for a separate reward model, and Kahneman-Tversky Optimization (KTO), which simplifies data collection further. To ensure safe deployment, 护栏(Guardrails) are implemented as a final safety layer to filter outputs and block harmful actions in real-time.", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:26:05.657183", "block_id": "ch29-b0011", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 642, "output_tokens": 234, "elapsed_sec": 3.15, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
{"block_id": "ch29-b0012", "type": "text", "source_sha256": "e175160cca76aa4b", "translated": "**Enhancing AI Agent Capabilities**\n\n**Chain of Thought (CoT)** This prompting technique encourages a model to explain its reasoning step-by-step before giving a final answer. This process of \"thinking out loud\" often leads to more accurate results on complex reasoning tasks.\n\n**Tree of Thoughts (ToT)** Tree of Thoughts is an advanced reasoning framework where an agent explores multiple reasoning paths simultaneously, like branches on a tree. It allows the agent to self-evaluate different lines of thought and choose the most promising one to pursue, making it more effective at complex problem-solving.\n\n**ReAct (Reason and Act)** ReAct is an agent framework that combines reasoning and acting in a loop. The agent first \"thinks\" about what to do, then takes an \"action\" using a tool, and uses the resulting observation to inform its next thought, making it highly effective at solving complex tasks.", "translate": true, "status": "translated", "usage": {"ts": "2026-08-09T10:26:07.485617", "block_id": "ch29-b0012", "chapter_id": 29, "model": "MiniMax-M3[1m]", "input_tokens": 4502, "output_tokens": 180, "elapsed_sec": 1.83, "stop_reason": "end_turn"}}
